WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.240
All right?
So, this is all a confusion in Gita.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.360
But whom to tell, you see?
You cannot tell them.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.320
Because you see they—actually,
it’s an attack on religion itself.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.200
In the beginning,
vegetarianism is an attack on religion.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:47.280
When Krishna had a cousin,
whose name was Neminath.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.320
And he was one of the tirthankaras
(ford-maker) of the Jains.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.320
But these people used to eat meat.
Meat was not regarded

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:59.040
as violence or anything.
And what happened, that, at this time,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.120
they attacked him [the attack came]
through this Neminath

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:08.320
because he saw many chickens being killed,
cattle being killed,

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.640
and he felt that mentally,
he felt compassion,

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.840
mental compassion for them.
And he said, "We should have

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:26.800
just ordinary food like carbohydrates."
And then, he told them,

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.000
"Better have [only] carbohydrates,
don’t eat any meat and things."

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.720
So, all this mental compassion
started from his cousin,

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.360
that was the first one.
But as a result of that,

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.015
they denounced Shri Krishna
because Krishna has some ‘Sanhaar shakti’.

00:01:38.015 --> 00:01:43.760
And Krishna being a Kshatriya,
he used to eat meat.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.240
So, they discarded him.
So, according to them,

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.760
Krishna was nothing but a ‘devyoni’.
He was nothing higher.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:53.600
These tirthankaras were higher, you see.
Actually, they are

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:58.400
the same Shambhalastas people.
Shambhala Gobi desert.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.200
That type of people. All right.
Whatever happened,

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.280
they discarded Shri Krishna at that time.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:10.240
At Rama’s time also, if you see,
Rama used to eat meat.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:17.280
Because, you see, his wife wanted a blouse
to be made out of the skin of a deer.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.840
I mean, it’s such a small petty thing.
For that, he wanted to kill the deer.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.240
That means he used to kill the deer
and eat it.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.880
And for making just a blouse,
if he can accept such a situation,

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.600
then he used to eat meat.
I mean, this is the proof of the pudding.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.640
And then after that, you see
Krishna, Rama, [inaudible]

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.120
and then Buddha also eat.
The surprising thing is,

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.080
in Buddha’s time,
just to show this perhaps,

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:48.160
Buddha went, at the end of his life,
he went to see one hunter.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:58.634
And the hunter had a—what you call—
a wild boar, a boar not cooked.

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:03.600
And it was not fully cooked.&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.720
So, the hunter told him,

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.840
"That’s not fully cooked,
and I’ve, I mean it was delayed."

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:11.360
He said, "It’s all right,
I have to go now. Better give me."

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:14.560
So, he ate that meat
and that’s how he died, you see.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.240
So, it is written down
that Buddha ate that wild boar [pork]

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.360
and he died of that.
So, this is a myth again

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.160
saying that he was a vegetarian.
He was not.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.520
His insight [unsure] meant
being kind to your fellow men.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.560
It’s a very funny idea,
diverting your attention

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.720
from human beings to other things.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.600
Of course, as we know,
we have common sense.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.600
In Sahaja Yoga,
we have to use common sense.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:41.600
And according to Sahaja Yoga, you see,
we don’t believe, indulge,

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.760
into all these melodramatic
compassion businesses, you see.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:54.000
So, in a proper way, what we do
is to find out, first of all,

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:59.840
what is the most important thing.
The most important thing

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:07.200
is to sustain human beings.
Because they are the most important,

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.400
they only can get Realization.
So, they are the most important.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.720
Now, how to sustain them?
Is to give them balanced food,

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:19.680
proper food, so that they are sustained
and they are good for Sahaja Yoga.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:26.080
We are not bothered about other animals.
Of course, we don’t eat animals

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:30.320
which are bigger than us
because their fibres can eat us up [unsure].

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:34.560
But if he eats even smaller animals—
actually, in the evolutionary process,

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.760
we give them a higher life.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.920
If you put into a bigger animal,
you will see,

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.000
it will take the shape
of the bigger animal.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:58.800
Muscular muscles or any muscles,
if you put it into the bigger animal,

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:03.440
the smaller one, you will see
that the muscles of the smaller animal

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:07.200
which you have introduced,
will take the shape of the bigger animal.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:13.360
This is—supposing,
a fish has to become a tortoise, all right?

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:20.160
Now, it must have
the muscles of the tortoise, isn’t it?

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.920
Now from where to get
the muscles of the tortoise?

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:27.040
So, to create these muscles
of the tortoise,

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.120
you have to put these fishes
into an animal

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:36.000
which will make them higher.
Once they are made higher animals,

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:42.960
then these animals, once they die,
they have greater muscular power

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.000
which can be used
and shared by lower animals.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.720
It’s common sense.
It’s common sense, you see.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.920
So, we also make provisions
for the lower animals.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:57.680
And the animals who are beyond us,
we do not eat.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:58.960
Because it is common sense.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:03.280
We use common sense;
we don’t use this melodramatic love

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:07.840
for the bugs, you see.
But we have common sense.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.880
By this common sense,
we stand in the centre

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:15.360
and we try to understand
how our body will be all right.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.520
And so doing—for example,
a person who just eats

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:23.440
vegetarianism food, what does he get?
All the troubles, you know,

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.120
Left Nabhi, first of all.
He can also get Left Swadishthana.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.480
But Left Nabhi is first.
And what is the result of a Left Nabhi

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:34.120
is that such a person
doesn’t have a proper digestion.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:37.440
The power in the muscles, in any muscle,
the muscles become very weak.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:46.480
So, such a person gets a muscle
which cannot throw the food in a proper way.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:48.560
So, all the time,
such a person gets diarrhoea.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:53.200
All the time. And then such a person
all the time feels hungry

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.960
and all the time gets diarrhoea.
It’s a very weak constitution

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:01.840
and such a person is very good,
vulnerable person for ‘bhoots’.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:08.320
Because it’s such a left-sided fellow.
Now, such a person can have also

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:15.120
a very sluggish liver.
So, he is very much susceptible to allergies.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:23.040
For example, in Gujarat,
people eat the same oil

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:27.760
that we eat in Maharashtra,
‘Shengdane’ (peanut).

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:31.920
But in Gujarat, if you go, I tell you,
at least, seventy percent people

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:36.080
have leucoderma [now] in the vessels.
The reason is that’s [that means that]

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:42.640
what people eat here,
the—what you call,

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:48.480
the fat of the groundnut,
which does not have much of proteins,

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:55.440
they become so susceptible
that they catch this leucoderma

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:58.640
much faster than the people
who eat meat in the Maharashtra.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:04.400
Because they cannot fight it.
So, they are suffering from leucoderma,

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:09.760
and this Left Nabhi can develop
with those people.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.400
Because, if you people have Left Nabhi,
it is because

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:19.480
it is an over-active Left Nabhi,
while they have a sluggish Left Nabhi.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:25.440
So, the people of the sluggish Left Nabhi
get all the problems

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.080
of the sluggish Left Nabhi
and it could be one of those

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:33.120
where you find
all the muscular disabilities

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:37.280
like myelitis and all those diseases.
What are the names of these diseases?

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:38.267
Muscular?

00:08:38.267 --> 00:08:43.311
Muscular these that start
degenerating muscles.

00:08:43.311 --> 00:08:47.807
Muscular degeneration.
Muscular dystrophy.

00:08:47.807 --> 00:08:48.904
Sclerosis.

00:08:48.903 --> 00:08:50.000
Sclerosis.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:54.663
All these diseases can come
through that kind of behaviour.

00:08:54.663 --> 00:08:58.698
Also, the leukaemia
and also the anaemias, Mother.

00:08:58.699 --> 00:08:59.440
Anaemia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:03.120
not leukaemia but anaemia.
And also, the children can be born

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:07.840
with that kind of a funny spleen,
which doesn’t produce any RBC’s.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:13.520
So, they have that kind of children,
they have that kind of problems,

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:16.320
and this and that.
So, to be one-sided like that

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:20.160
is stupid according to Sahaja Yoga.
There is no need to be

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.000
that kind of compassionate person.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:27.360
In this country, because lack of money,
so many people are vegetarians.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:37.120
Now, for example, people, say,
from Bihar, suffer from a disease

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:40.240
called ‘beriberi’.
If they eat proteins, they will never

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:44.320
have beriberi trouble, you see.
Because this B-complex and all that,

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:52.080
whatever they may say, if you eat meat
then B-complex is compensated.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.480
So, because they cannot afford
to eat meat,

00:09:54.480 --> 00:10:00.000
they just eat vegetable oil
and things like that.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:08.320
Mustard oil. And with that
they do not get any protein within themselves,

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.400
they suffer from that.
So, all these diseases

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.840
of our country can be solved.

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.960
Like, also, we have
a disease of the lungs—

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:22.160
what you call that—
TB,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:30.000
tuberculosis.

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:36.960
That also comes from the same problem.
And the, also, the trouble

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:45.840
of the Left Vishuddhi.
And this Left Vishuddhi troubles are,

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:48.240
could be—what you call—&nbsp;

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:53.680
Left Vishuddhi and Left Nabhi,

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:56.960
if they join,
they form the disease of

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:01.700
from liver—rheumatism.
Rheumatism and another is,

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:05.681
that comes on the joints,
what do you call?

00:11:05.681 --> 00:11:06.629
Arthritis.

00:11:06.629 --> 00:11:11.558
Arthritis.
This is also Left [Nabhi, Left Vishuddhi],

00:11:11.559 --> 00:11:13.360
these two combines.&nbsp;

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.960
And also, this—what you call—

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:17.120
this spondylosis.
Spondylosis, spondylosis.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:25.600
Spondylitis is something different.
Also, spondylitis, I would say,

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:30.600
the whole of, whole of your muscles
can go into tantrum [unsure].

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:38.480
And for the brain: madness.
Schizophrenic or mad,

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:41.840
such people can become mad because,
what happens with them,

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:47.040
is that they are vulnerable
to the left-side attacks.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.160
So, they can become mad.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.960
The worse is heart.
They get a heart which is sluggish,

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:58.400
which—angina—what is the, you see,
all these things which require

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:03.600
pumping of the blood better,
like coarctation and what else is there?

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:07.920
Low blood pressure, Mother.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:11.360
Yes, low blood pressure.
And also—what you call—the

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:13.520
The [inaudible] problem.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:21.120
And also, could be paralysis;
paralysis you can get

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:25.440
because if the clot is
with low blood pressure, you see,

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:29.040
it fixes up itself.
And such people clot their blood

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:29.600
very easily.

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:35.364
What about [unclear: arteriosclerosis
hardening of the arteries] the heart?

00:12:35.364 --> 00:12:35.640
Yes, of course.
That too [unclear]

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:36.000
[hardening of the arteries]
of the heart is,

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.000
all these things go
[hand in hand].

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:49.120
All right. So, you see,
we have to be sensible people,

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:52.320
we are not to work out ourselves
through our brain power

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:55.040
but through our spiritual power,
means the Spirit.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.520
And when the Spirit says, "It’s all right"
we should see.

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:59.840
Such people sometimes,
I’ve seen they are numb.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:03.840
And their hands feel so cool
that they feel that it is vibrations.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:07.040
It’s not so.
They are absolutely numb people

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:09.680
and they cannot feel anything.
I mean, like death,

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:11.680
a person who is going to die.

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:17.360
Once I was treating a lady
and I had such numbness on my left-side

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:20.080
that I got a fright of my life.
I said, "This lady is going to die

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:22.880
or what, what’s the problem with her?"
So, I found out

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:26.160
she was a strict vegetarian.
She would not even take—

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:29.680
what you call—garlic
and would not even touch any—

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:30.925
[Inaudible].

00:13:30.925 --> 00:13:34.960
And I think some Rakshasa
must have introduced this

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:40.240
because all the Rakshasas whom we know,
say, Maheshyogi, say Rajneesh,

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:41.114
say this [unclear], Bhandasur [unclear].

00:13:41.114 --> 00:13:41.405
The fat little boy?

00:13:41.405 --> 00:13:48.788
No, no, Bhandasur is Muktananda.

00:13:48.788 --> 00:13:49.736
Muktananda.

00:13:49.735 --> 00:13:52.750
Muktananda.
Bhandasur is Muktananda.

00:13:52.751 --> 00:13:58.092
Then this fat little boy who’s there
is Raktabija [Red drop].

00:13:58.092 --> 00:14:01.280
You see, all of them are vegetarians,&nbsp;

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:01.920
surprisingly!

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:06.560
All of them are vegetarians,
none of them is non-vegetarian.

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:08.400
This Vaswani,
this [inaudible] all of them.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:14.800
They are all vegetarian.
And they are always preaching,

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:20.320
"We should be kind to the animals
and we should be kind to this,"

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:20.833
all sort of nonsense.

00:14:20.833 --> 00:15:23.840
Give bandhan to Manore.
You see, it happens like that.

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.840
One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:53.200
gentleman who is a big—
that same fellow partner.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:56.720
He wants to give a program. All right.
So, we can’t cancel our program.

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.520
I said, "Now don’t."
They have already cancelled.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:02.000
I said, "We like that Manore program,
we’ll all go there."

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:07.840
Whatever it is, howsoever people
you might get, we’ll go for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:21.840
it.

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:16.720
There’s only one advantage of science
is that every country

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:22.560
is afraid of each other.
That’s the advantage we have reached

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:26.480
of science which we must accept.
You see, we must congratulate them

00:20:26.480 --> 00:20:29.440
for this great thing
that they are all frightened

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:32.400
of each other.
America is frightened of Russia.

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:33.944
Russia is frightened of America.
That’s a very big thing, you see,

00:20:33.944 --> 00:20:40.535
that they are frightened of each other.
So, they are not fighting

00:20:40.535 --> 00:20:42.080
and keep apart.&nbsp;

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:44.160
They have created this monster

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:46.760
and now they are afraid
of the monster itself.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:50.560
This is like that Frankenstein, you know?

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:57.280
That I felt that Frankenstein
is very symbolic picture

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:02.840
which shows that you made a man
who started eating you off.

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:08.560
All right.
Now have you had your dinner, lunch?

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:09.760
Maybe [inaudible].

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:33.200
Now the second part is to go
and I would also like to go.

